The troubles of this world seem to never fade. They shift, change, and reform, but they are ever-present.

The wind brought us whispers of a traitor in our midst. We sent one of our best sentinels to investigate, and now she has turned up dead. I did her disservice in assuming that the traitor would not be aware of our movements... I was brash, and she paid for my folly.

I need a new face to pick up the trail. Someone the people of the city won't know. This is a dangerous request. Will you help me? 
